## Severity vs. Detectability Matrix

```
                    LOW DETECTABILITY    HIGH DETECTABILITY
                   ┌─────────────────────┬──────────────────┐
HIGH IMPACT        │ P1 🔴 P3 🔴        │ P6 🟡  P7 🟢    │
                   │ P10🔴 P9 🟡        │                  │
                   ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────┤
MODERATE IMPACT    │ P2 🟡 P5 🟢        │  P4 🟢  P8 🟢   │
                   │                     │                  │
                   └─────────────────────┴──────────────────┘
```

**Key insight:** The upper-left quadrant — high impact, low detectability — contains the patterns most likely to cause real operational damage before anyone identifies a problem. This quadrant should drive evaluation prioritization.

